WEBVTT

00:11:29.676 --> 00:11:32.636
was supposed to be able
to help close that gap

00:11:32.636 --> 00:11:35.116
and help families offset the cost.

00:11:35.116 --> 00:11:38.356
Now, the government, Congress
has said sorry, not sorry,

00:11:38.396 --> 00:11:40.076
not passing the bill, right?

00:11:40.556 --> 00:11:44.796
So the private sector
is the only other institution

00:11:44.836 --> 00:11:47.676
that can come in here and fix the model.

00:11:47.676 --> 00:11:49.556
When the private sector starts saying,

00:11:49.556 --> 00:11:53.356
"OK, we are going to start
offering childcare subsidies,

00:11:53.356 --> 00:11:55.236
backup care, emergency care,

00:11:55.276 --> 00:11:57.036
we're going to build daycare centers,

00:11:57.076 --> 00:12:01.796
when they basically take responsibility
for fixing the business model,